# Everything, then back in only what the server reads at run time. A denylist
# would have let the next wiki dump into the image without anyone noticing.
*
!server/
!data/

# Build inputs, not run-time tables: the raw wiki dumps the data/build_*.py
# scripts were fed, 15 MB of pages nothing imports.
data/wiki/
data/wiki_world/

# The database belongs on a volume. Copying a development one in would have it
# shadowed by the mount at best, and shipped with accounts in it at worst.
# A wildcard, not three names: the copies kept beside it before a risky step
# (lava.db.before-archivist and its -wal/-shm) went into the image otherwise.
data/lava.db*

**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
